  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying the sure outcome (minimum absolute value), computing differences from it, and summing weighted differences. While the individual does identify the zero outcome as special (which aligns with the 'sure outcome' concept), they do not compute or reference any differences from this outcome or their probabilistic weights. Instead, the justification is solely based on the higher probability of achieving the zero outcome in Lottery B. The decision reason involves a more complex evaluation that includes all outcomes and their deviations, but the individual only considers the probability of one outcome. There is partial alignment in recognizing 0 as a focal point, but no evidence of applying the full rule involving weighted differences. Therefore, the individual did not use the specified decision reason, even though they focused on a related aspect (the zero outcome).",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
